    <div class="sg-section">
      <div class="sg-title">Buttons</div>
      <p class="sg-desc">Every button is at least 44 by 44 pixels, with a visible focus ring and WCAG AA contrast in every state. Hover darkens primary buttons, inverts outline buttons, and never lowers contrast.</p>

      <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;font-size:1.05rem">Primary (default call-to-action)</h3>
      <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:0.35rem;margin-bottom:0.85rem">Navy background, white text. On hover, the navy deepens. Used for the main button, such as "Start now," on light sections.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem">
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-primary">Default</a>
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-primary" style="background:var(--navy-950);border-color:var(--navy-950);color:#fff;transform:translateY(-1px)">Hover</a>
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Default (large)</a>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;font-size:1.05rem">Gold (on dark backgrounds)</h3>
      <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:0.35rem;margin-bottom:0.85rem">Gold background, navy text. On hover, the gold lightens. Used inside navy hero sections and call-to-action bands. The text is always navy, because white on gold fails contrast.</p>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem;background:var(--navy-900);border-radius:var(--radius);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem">
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-gold">Default</a>
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-gold" style="background:var(--gold-400);border-color:var(--gold-400);color:var(--navy-900);transform:translateY(-1px)">Hover</a>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;font-size:1.05rem">Outline (dark)</h3>
      <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:0.35rem;margin-bottom:0.85rem">Transparent background with a navy border and navy text. On hover, navy fills in and the text turns white. Used for a second button on light sections.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem">
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-outline-dark">Default</a>
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-outline-dark" style="background:var(--navy-900);color:#fff">Hover</a>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;font-size:1.05rem">Light outline (on dark)</h3>
      <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:0.35rem;margin-bottom:0.85rem">Transparent with a white border. On hover, a faint white tint fills in. Used inside hero sections and call-to-action bands.</p>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem;background:var(--navy-900);border-radius:var(--radius);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem">
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-outline">Default</a>
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-outline" style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.12);border-color:#fff">Hover</a>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;font-size:1.05rem">Ghost (tertiary)</h3>
      <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:0.35rem;margin-bottom:0.85rem">No background or border. Used for low-emphasis links that still need a click target.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem">
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-ghost">Default</a>
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-ghost" style="background:var(--bg-alt-2);color:var(--navy-900)">Hover</a>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-top:1.5rem;font-size:1.05rem">Contrast rules</h3>
      <ul style="font-size:0.93rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0.5rem 0 0 1.25rem">
        <li>Text against its background: always 4.5:1 or better (AA for normal text), and at least 3:1 for large display text.</li>
        <li>Hover states never lower contrast below the default state.</li>
        <li>Navy buttons in the main menu must not pick up the menu-link hover background, which is why that hover applies only to <code>a:not(.btn)</code>.</li>
        <li>Gold buttons always pair with navy text, and navy buttons always pair with white text.</li>
        <li>The focus state on every button is a gold outline ring with a 3px offset.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sg-section">
